hadiths[40]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4257","Ismail bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Husayn bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Shihab bin Abdul Rabbo, on the authority of Omar bin Ali, who said: I walked with Muhammad bin Ali, and he said: I bear witness that my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, “God Almighty made His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, live in Mecca for thirteen years.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “The narrations agreed on these matters with the narrations they narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. As for the narration of Anas, And Muawiyah, even if their chains of transmission are authentic within ten years, then they are not obligated to say or act.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4257 - True"
"4258","Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Issa bin Ubaid Al-Kindi told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Abdullah Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah bin Amr, on the authority of Jarir, that the Prophet said: “God Almighty revealed to me which of these The three countries you settled in are the places of your emigration: Medina, Bahrain, or Qinnasrin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4258 - True"
"4259","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Mecca, so he was ordered to migrate.” And it was revealed to him: “And say, ‘My Lord, admit me to an entrance of truth, and bring me out to a exit of truth, and give me from Yourself an authority and helper.’” [Al-Isra: 80] “This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4259 - True"
"4260","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Husayn bin Muhammad Al-Maruzi told us, Shayban bin Abd told us The Most Gracious, on the authority of Qatada, the Almighty, the Almighty: {And say, “My Lord, let me enter an entrance of truthfulness and bring me out a exit of truthfulness.” [Al-Isra: 80] “So God brought him out of Mecca to Medina is the exit of truthfulness, and his entry into Medina is the entrance of truthfulness.” He said: “And the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew that there is no power He has no authority in this matter except with authority, so he asked for authority to support the Book of God and the limits of God, and the obligations of God, and to establish the Book of God, and that “Sultan is an honor from God, whom He has placed among the backs of His servants. Were it not for that, some of them would attack others, and the strong would devour the weak.”"
"4261","Professor Abu Al-Walid and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Musa Al-Ansari told us, Saad told us Ibn Sa`id al-Maqbari, my brother told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, you You took me out of the country I love most, so put me in the country I love most.” So God placed him in Medina. “This is a hadith narrated by Madanis from the family of Abu Saeed Al-Maqbari»
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4261 - But it is a topic"
"4262","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the Muslims: “I have been shown the place of your migration. I have been shown a marsh. of palm trees between two trees” and they are the two free ones. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4262 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4263","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Khalil al-Tustari told us, Kathir bin Yahya told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Ali himself fell ill, and he wore the garment of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and then he slept.” in his place, and the polytheists were accusing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had clothed him with a cloak, and it was Quraysh wanted to kill the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so they started shooting at Ali, and they saw that he was the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he had worn a cloak, and Ali May God be pleased with him, he was starving, and then it was Ali. They said: You are a mean person. You should be starving. And your companion was not starving, and we disapproved of him. From you: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi and others, on the authority of Abu Awanah, with additional wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4263 - True"
"4264","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Ubaid bin Qunfud al-Bazzar told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid al-Hamani told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’, Hakim bin Jubayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, who said: “The first to buy himself seeking the pleasure of God was Ali bin Abi Talib,” and he said Ali when he slept on the bed of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a poem
 [Long Sea]

 I have protected myself from something better than the one who stepped on pebbles... and the one who circumambulated the Ancient House and the stones.
 A messenger of a god who feared that they would plot against him... So Dhu Al-Tall saved him from the plot.
 And the Messenger of God spent the night in the cave, secure... protected, under the protection of God, and under cover.
 I spent the night looking after them and they did not accuse me... I had trained myself to kill and capture.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4264 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4265","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Musa al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Dawud told us, Nu’aym bin Hakim told us, Abu Maryam told us Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: On the night that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to spend the night in his bed, and he went out Migrating from Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took me to the idols and said: “Sit.” So I sat next to the Kaaba, then he went up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on my shoulders and then said: “Get up.” So I got up with him, and when he saw my weakness beneath him, he said: Sit down, so I sat down. So I took him down from me, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sat for me, and then he said to me: “O Ali, climb on my shoulders.” So I climbed on his shoulders, and then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up with me, and it seemed to me that if I wanted, I could reach heaven, and ascended to the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stepped aside. So I threw their largest idol, which was made of copper and attached to iron pegs, to the ground. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: He said: “Treat him,” so I treated him and I am still treating him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Eh, eh,” so I continued treating him until I was able From it, he said: “He checked it,” so I checked it, broke it, and revealed “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"4266","Ali bin Muhammad al-Hammadi told us about Marwa, Abu Ya’qub Ishaq bin Ibrahim al-Sarkhasi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Alqamah al-Marwazi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet prayed God, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him: “Who will migrate with me? He said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and text, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4266 - Sahih Gharib"
"4267","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them, she said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, headed He arrived from Mecca to Medina, and with him was Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr carried with him all his money, five thousand or six thousand dirhams, so my grandfather came to me. Abu Quhafa, whose sight had gone, said: By God, this man has given you his wealth along with his own soul. I said: No, father, he left it to us. It was very good, so I took stones and placed them in the alcove of the house, where Abu Bakr used to put his money, and I covered the stones. With a garment, then I came and took his hand and placed it on the garment, and he said: As for if he left this, then yes. She said: “By God, he did not leave a little.” “Not much.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4267 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4268","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Al-Sari bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Sirin told us, He said: He mentioned men during the reign of Omar, may God be pleased with him, as if they preferred Omar over Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them. He said: This reached Omar. May God be pleased with him, and he said: By God, a night of Abu Bakr is better than the family of Omar, and a day of Abu Bakr is better than the family of Omar. The Messenger of God has gone out. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he went to the cave with Abu Bakr. He walked for an hour in front of him and an hour behind him, until the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, noticed him. He, peace be upon him, said: “O Abu Bakr, why do you walk for an hour in front of me and an hour behind me?” He said: O Messenger of God, remember the request and walk behind you, then remember the lookout and walk in front of you. He said: O Abu Bakr, if anything Did you like to be without me? He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth, you would not have known anything except that you were with me rather than you. So when they reached the cave, Abu Bakr said: Your place, O Messenger of God, until the cave was cleared for you. So he entered and cleared it until, when he was at the top, he mentioned that he had not cleared it. The room, and he said: Your place, O Messenger of God, until he cleared the room, so he entered and cleared the room, then he said: Come down, O Messenger of God, so he came down and said Omar: By the One in whose hand is my soul that night, he is better than the family of Omar. He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4268 - Sahih mursal"
"4269","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Asbahani told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm bin Jabla Al-Taymi told us, Musa bin Al-Mashawar, Abdullah bin Muadh Al-Sana’ani told us, on the authority of Muammar bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Malik Al-Mudaliji told me, He is the nephew of Suraqa bin Jasham. His father told him that he heard Suraqa bin Jasham saying: The messengers of the infidels of Quraysh have come to us. They imposed on the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, a blood money for each one of them, for whoever killed them or captured them. While I was sitting in One of my people’s gatherings, from Bani Mudlij, a man came from them until he rose up against us and said: O Suraqa, I just saw lions on the coast. I saw it as Muhammad and his companions. Suraqa said: Then I knew it was them, so I told them: They were not among them, but I saw so-and-so and so-and-so departing. Unjustly, he said: Then I remained in the assembly for only an hour until I got up and entered my house, so I ordered my maid to bring out my horse to me while she was behind me. And I took my spear and went out from the back of the house, and I planned to cast it into the ground, and I held the spear high until I brought my horse, mounted it, and raised it to come closer to me until I saw their blackness.When I approached them, where they heard the sound, my horse stumbled at me, so I fell off her, so I got up and lowered my hand to my quiver, so I extracted The reins, so I swore by them, and the one who hated not to harm them came out, so I disobeyed the reins, so I mounted my horse and raised her to come near me until When I approached them, “I heard the recitation of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not turn around,” and Abu Bakr turned around a lot, so my horse’s hands became stuck in the ground until they reached the knees, so I fell down from her, then I rebuked her, and she got up, but she could hardly take out her hands. When she stood upright, there was a trace of Her hands are bright clouds in the sky - Abdullah said: meaning the smoke that comes from without fire - then I took out the arrows, and divided them with them. So the one who hated not to harm them came out, so I called them to be safe and they stopped, so I rode my horse until I came to them, and I fell into myself when I met someone... imprisonment for them until the matter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would become known. So I said to him: Your people have imposed blood money on you, and I informed them of News of their journey, and what the people wanted about them. I offered them provisions and goods, but they did not ask me anything, and they did not ask me except to say: Hide from us. So I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to write me a letter of farewell that I would believe in.“Then Aamir bin Fuhayrah, Abu Bakr’s servant, ordered me to write to me on a piece of paper and then they went on: ‘This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4269 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4270","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Adi bin Al-Hamra’ Al-Zuhri, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on his camel. In a hazura, he says: “By God, you are the best of God’s land, and the most beloved of God’s land to God, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4270 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4271","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Ali bin Saeed told me, Yunus bin Habib told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left Mecca, Abu Bakr said: {To Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return} [Al-Baqarah: 156] The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent out to destroy us. He said: So it was revealed. This verse: {Permission has been given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and indeed, God is Able to grant them victory. Those who have been expelled from their homes unjustly} [Al-Hajj: 40], Abu Bakr knew that there would be a fight. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"4272","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil ibn Khalaf al-Qadi told us, Musa ibn Ishaq al-Qadi informed us, Masruq ibn al-Marzban told us, Yahya ibn Zakaria told us. Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Ibn Ishaq said, Muhammad Ibn Ja`far Ibn Al-Zubayr told me, and Muhammad Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abdullah Ibn Hussein, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left the cave, migrating And with him were Abu Bakr and Amer bin Fuhayra. Abu Bakr was his successor, and Abdullah bin Uriqat Al-Laythi succeeded him, so he took them down from Mecca. Then he proceeded with them until he landed with them on the coast below Usfan, then he passed with them at the bottom of Amja, then he returned to the road after he had passed. A long time ago, then he took them through the Hijaz, then he passed through the Thaniyat al-Marar with them, then he took them through Al-Hafiyah, then he passed through the Madlijat of Qaf with them, Then he rode with them, with a flat stomach, then with a flat stomach with them, then with a flat stomach, like Dhul-Ghusun, then with a firm stomach, then He took the jilbab, then he took a ladder from the stomach to the top of the mudlaj, then he took the qāḥa, then he descended the limp, then he took the gharī’s fold, To the right of his riding, then Raym’s belly descended and he presented Quba’ to Banu Amr bin Awf. This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s condition, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4272 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4273","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Ubayd Allah bin Iyad bin Laqit told us, Iyad bin Laqit told us, on the authority of Qays bin Al-Numan, he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr set off concealing themselves, they passed by a servant tending sheep, so they gave him milk to drink, and he said: I do not have a sheep. She is being milked, but here is a she-camel that became pregnant at the beginning of winter, and it has given birth and has no milk left. So he said: “Call for her.” So they called for her, so he arrested her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped her udder and prayed until she came down. He said: Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, came with a shield and milked Abu Bakr, then He milked and gave the shepherd water to drink, then he milked and drank, and the shepherd said: By God, who are you? By God, I have never seen anyone like you. He said: Or do you think you are keeping secret from me to the point of Did I tell you? He said: Yes. He said: “For I am Muhammad, the Messenger of God.” He said: “You are the one whom the Quraysh claim is a Sabian.” He said: “They say that.” He said: So I bear witness that you are a prophet, and I bear witness that what you have brought is the truth, and that no one will do what you have done except a prophet, and I am following you. He said: “You do not “You can do that on your day, so when you hear that I have appeared, come to us.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4273 - True"
"4274","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told us, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Khazzaz told us, Suleiman bin Al-Hakam bin Ayyub bin Sulaiman bin Thabit bin Bashar Al-Khuza’i, my brother Ayyub bin Al-Hakam, and Salem bin Muhammad Al-Khuza’i all told us, on the authority of Hazzam bin Hisham, on the authority of his father Hisham bin Hubaysh bin Khuwaylid, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He left Mecca, migrating to Medina, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and Abu Bakr’s servant was Amer bin Fuhayra, and their guide Al-Laythi Abdullah bin Uriqat They passed by the tent of Umm Ma’abad Al-Khuza’iyya, and there was a bare-faced woman who was sheltering in the courtyard of the tent, then watering And she was fed, so they asked her for meat and dates to buy from her, but they did not get any of that, and the people were old widows, so the Messenger of God looked God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked at a sheep in the tent, and said: “What is this sheep, O Umm Ma’abad?” She said: A sheep that was left behind from the sheep. He said: “Does it have any milk?” She said: She is more tired than that. He said: Do you permit me to milk her? She said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. If you see milk in it, milk it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for it.So he wiped her udder with his hand, and called upon God Almighty, and supplicated for her regarding her sheep, and she turned to him, turning, and chewing her cud. He called for a vessel in which the flock would lie down, and he milked them. Therein was snow until he was radiant, then he watered it until it was quenched, and he gave his companions to drink until it was quenched, and the last of them drank until they were satisfied, then he milked the second time in it. He went on calmly until he filled the vessel, then he left her there, then she pledged allegiance to her and they departed from her. She did not stay long until her husband, Abu, came to her. Ma'bad drove two lean goats, both of them emaciated and with a little disfigurement. When Abu Ma'bad saw the milk, he was impressed with it. He said: Where did you get this, mother? A temple, and the sheep is single and isolated, and there is no dairy in the house? She said: No, by God, except that a blessed man passed by us in such and such a condition. He said: Describe him for me, O Umm Ma’abad. She said: I saw a man who appeared He is well-groomed, has a beautiful face, has a good disposition, he is not afflicted by sluggishness, nor is he affected by a baldness. He is handsome and handsome, with a dent in his eyes and on his labia. He neighed, and there was a neigh in his voice, and there was a brightness in his neck, and in his beard there were thick streaks of white hair. If he kept silent, he would be revered, and if he spoke, he would be praised. And above Him is splendor, the most beautiful and most impressive of people from afar, and the best and most beautiful from near, sweet in logic and clear, without trifle or nonsense. Its girth is as if it were stringed beads, descending into a quadrimeter without any length.Not a single eye can pierce him through a palace, a branch between two branches, for he is the brightest in appearance and the best of the three, and he is destined to have companions who surround him. He said: They listened to what he said, and if he gave a command, they hastened to give him his command. Mahfud and gathered together, neither frowning nor disapproving. Abu Ma’bad said: This is God’s companion. The Quraysh, whose affairs were mentioned to us, and I intended to accompany him, and I will do so if I find a way to do so, and a voice became High up in Mecca, they heard the voice, but did not know who it was, saying:
 [Long Sea]

 May God, the Lord of mankind, reward them well...two companions who settled in the tents of Umm Ma’abad.
 They sent down guidance to her and she was guided by it... So he who became Muhammad’s companion was victorious.
 What a story, what God has withheld from you... He has done good deeds that cannot be rewarded and repaid.
 May Abu Bakr enjoy his grandfather’s happiness... With his company, whoever makes God happy makes him happy.
 The Banu Ka'b will have the place of their girl... and her seat will be for the believers in an ambush.
 Ask your sister about her sheep and her vessel... for if you ask a sheep, she will bear witness.
 He called her a stray sheep, and she milked... against him, openly declaring the harm of the sheep. More
 So he left him as a mortgage to her to Haleb... He repeats it in source after source.
 . When Hassan heard that, he started answering the phone and said:
 [Long Sea]

 A people have been disappointed because their Prophet has disappeared from them...And sanctify those who go to them and have lunch.
 He departed from a people whose minds were lost...and came upon a people with renewed light.
 Their Lord guided them thereby after misguidance...so He who follows the truth guides them.
 Is the misguidance of a foolish people equal to blindness and those guided by someone who is guided?
 And it descended from it upon the people of Yathrib... the riders of guidance descended upon them with As’ad.
 A prophet who sees what the people around him do not see... and recites the Book of God in every scene.
 And if he says something in absentia one day...then you must believe it on the same day or in the morning tomorrow.”
 This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” Its authenticity and the truthfulness of its narrators are proven by evidence, including the descent of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the two tents, it has been repeatedly mentioned in authentic and numerous narrations, including that those who narrated the hadith according to its face are the people of the two tents, among the Bedouins who They are not accused of fabricating the hadith and adding or subtracting from it, and they took it word after word on the authority of Abu Ma’abad and Umm Ma’abad, including that It has chains of narrations such as taking by the hand. The child was taken from his father, and the father from his grandfather. There is no transmission or weakness in the narrators, among them is that Al-Hurr ibn Al-Sabbah Al-Nakha'i took it from Abu Ma'abad, just as his son took it from him.As for the chain of transmission that we narrated in the context of the hadith about the Ka’bis, it is a correct and high chain of transmission for the Bedouin Arabs, and they were superior to us in the hadith. Al-Hurr bin Al-Sabbah
 [p. 12]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4274 - True"
"4275","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, going back to the beginning. Al-Hussein bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, Abu Ahmad Bishr bin Muhammad Al-Sukkari told me, Abd al-Malik ibn Wahb al-Madhaji told us, al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah al-Nakha’i told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad al-Khuza’i, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out One night he greeted a migrant, and he mentioned the hadith in its length, like the hadith of Sulaiman ibn al-Hakam. As for the hadith of the two tents, which is known for its narrations, it was"
"4276","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, and Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Suwar told me, and Abd told me Allah bin Muhammad al-Dawrqi, among others, they said: Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Imam told us, and Mukhalid bin Ja`far al-Baqarhi told me, Muhammad bin Jarir told us, They said: Mukarram bin Mahrez told us, then I heard the righteous Sheikh Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Jaafar bin Hamdan al-Bazzar al-Quti’i, saying: Mukarram bin Mahrez, on the authority of his father, “Then they mentioned the hadith in its length, similar to the hadith of Abu Ma’bad, so I said to our sheikh Abu Bakr Al-Quta’i: The sheikh heard it from Honored? He said: Yes, by God, my father performed Hajj on me when I was seven years old, so he brought me in to see Mukarram bin Mahrez.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4276 - There is nothing in these methods that meets the condition of correctness"
"4277","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Musa bin Al-Mashawir told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mashawar told us Muadh al-Sana’ani, Muammar ibn Rashid told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr told me that he heard al-Zubayr mention, “He met the caravan of The Muslims were merchants in the Levant, traveling from Mecca. They opposed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr wearing white clothes when they heard of their departure. When the Muslims in Medina heard of the departure of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they went to Al-Harrah every morning and waited for him until The heat of the afternoon hurt them, so they turned one day after waiting for him for a long time. When they had gone to their homes, a Jewish man fulfilled his burden. He looked at them to look at it, and he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions shining brightly, with the mirage removed from them. The Jew did not have the power to He said in his loudest voice: O Arabs, this is your companion whom you are waiting for. So the Muslims rose up to arms and met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4277 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4278","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the Mosque of Banu Amr Ibn Awf, which is the Quba Mosque, to pray in it. Then men from the Ansar entered and greeted him. Ibn Umar said: Suhaib entered with them, so I asked him how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was. What does he do if someone greets him while he is praying? He said: “He was gesturing with his hand.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4278 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4279","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Maru, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi told us Osama, Muhammad bin Issa bin al-Tabba’ told us, Muja’ bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sulayman al-Hazami told me, he said: I heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif narrates, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque - meaning the Quba Mosque - and prays “Therein it was like the reward of ‘Umrah.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4279 - True"
"4280","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali told us Ibn Abdullah Al-Madani, Hammad bin Usama told us, Hashim bin Hashim told us, he said: I heard Amer bin Saad and Aisha bint Saad saying: We heard Saad say: “Because I pray in the Mosque of Quba is more beloved to me than praying in the Mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4280 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4281","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Radi God Almighty said: “I witnessed the day the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Medina, and I have never seen a day better or brighter than it.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4281 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4282","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proceeded until he came to Medina and came out people until we entered the road, and the women, servants, and boys shouted, “Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has come. God is great, Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has come.” When the morning became “He set off and descended where he was commanded.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4282 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4283","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf bin Abi Jamila told us, on the authority of Zurara bin Abu Awfa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, the people rushed to him, and it was said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: I came among the people to look, and when I recognized his face, I knew that his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him speak was when he said: “O people, spread greetings, provide food, maintain ties of kinship, and pray while the people sleep.” “You will enter Paradise in peace.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4283 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4284","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Nu`aym bin Hammad told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Hashraj bin Nabatah told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Juman, on the authority of the ship of the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built the mosque, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, brought a stone and placed it, then Omar came with a stone and placed it, then Othman brought a stone and placed it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “These are the rulers after me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4284 - True"
"4285","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Khayyat told us in Baghdad, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz told us, Abu Muammar told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi told us Hazim, on the authority of his father Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The people made a mistake in counting. They did not count his pledge of allegiance, nor counted his death. Introduction to Medina “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4285 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4286","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Sahl told us Muslim, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The date was in the year in which the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to “And he handed over the city and in it Abdullah bin Al-Zubair was born.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4286 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4287","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Othman bin Ubayd Allah Abi Rafi’ said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: He gathered the ages of the people and asked them on what day was history written? Ali bin Abi Talib said: “From the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, emigrated and left the land of polytheism,” so Omar, may God be pleased with him, did this. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4287 - True"
"4288","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl, in Baghdad, informed us. Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Ali bin told us. Coming, Ali bin Salih bin Hayy told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Jumay bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: When it was narrated The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood among his companions in Medina. Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, came with tears in his eyes and said: O Messenger of God, you made a brotherhood between Your friends and you did not create friendship between me and anyone. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ali, you are my brother in this world and the hereafter.” Salem continued. Ibn Abi Hafsa, on the authority of all, with an addition in the context"
"4289","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Nahwi told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi told us, Ishaq ibn Bishr told us Al-Kahili, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Juma bin Umair al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother among his companions. He was a brother between Abu Bakr and Omar, between Talha and al-Zubayr, and between Uthman bin Affan and Abd. Al-Rahman bin Awf, then Ali said: O Messenger of God, you have shown brotherhood among your companions, so who is my brother? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Are you not satisfied, O Ali, with me being your brother?” Ibn Omar said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, was a brave man. Ali said: Yes, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You My brother in this world and the hereafter.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4289 - Juma bin Umair was accused and Ishaq bin Bishr Al-Kahili perished."
"4290","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl, and Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Qattan told us, saying: Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Ali bin Asim told us, On the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb, and Ali bin Issa told me, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Jurashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ali bin Yahya told us Mushahir, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad, he said: Talha Al-Basri narrated to me, saying: A man was one of us when he came In the city, he had a sergeant there who descended upon his sergeant, and if he did not have a sergeant there, he descended in a row. So I came and the row descended upon us, and he used to run over us from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a mudd of dates every day, and they covered us with the sheep. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led some prayers with us. daytime prayer. When he said the salaam, the people of Suffah called to him right and left: O Messenger of God, the dates have burned our stomachs, and the sheep have been torn from us. So the Messenger of God turned away. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he went to his pulpit and ascended it, thanking God and praising Him. Then he mentioned the hardship he faced from his people until he said: “And he came I and my companion have a dozen, and neither I nor him have any food except Al-Barir.” He said: I said to Abu Harb: What is Al-Barir? He said: The food of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Arak dates. “So we presented these to our brothers from the Ansar, and the bulk of their food was dates, and they consoled us.” In it, by God, if I had found bread and meat for you, I would have satisfied you with it. But perhaps you will reach a time when one of you will be served as lunch with a handful. And he will be comforted with another.” He said: They said: O Messenger of God, is we better today or that day? He said: “Rather, today you are better. Today you love one another, but on that day you will strike each other’s necks.” I see it. He said: “Hot enemies.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Sahl al-Qattan, and the hadith of Yahya bin Yahya in brief. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4290 - True"
"4291","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, Mujahid told us, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: The people of Suffah were the guests of Islam and did not come to any family or money, and by God, there is no god but It is if I used to support my liver on the ground because of hunger, and I used to put a stone on my stomach because of hunger, and one day I sat on the back of their road. On which they would go out, Abu Bakr passed by me and I asked him about a verse from the Book of God. I only asked him so that he would follow me, so he passed by and did not do so, then he passed by Omar, so I asked him about a verse from the Book of God Almighty. I only asked him so that he could follow me. He passed by and did not do so. Then Abu al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by. He greeted me and smiled when he saw me, and said: “Abu Hurairah.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “The truth.” He went on, so I followed him and he entered his house. So I asked him for permission, and he allowed me. He found milk in a cup and said: “Where did you get this milk?” It was said: So-and-so gave it to us, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Abu Hurairah.” So I said: Here you are. He said: “The people of Suffah are right, so call them.” They are the guests of Islam, they do not provide accommodation for family or property. If someone gives him charity, he sends it to them, but he does not take any of it. And when a gift came to him, he sent it to them and received some of it, and shared it with them. That upset me, and I said: What is this disgrace among the people of Suffah? And I am his messenger to them, so he commands me to turn it over to them. What might happen to me from it, when I was hoping that something from it would happen to me that would enrich me? It was necessary to obey God and obey His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I came to them and called them, and when they entered upon him and took As they sat, he said: “Abu Hurr, take the cup and give it to them.” So I took the cup and gave it to the man, so he drank until he was satisfied, then returned it. I handed him the other and he drank until I brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and all the people had narrated it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it. He handed over the cup to him and placed it on his hands. Then he raised his head to me and smiled, and said: “O Abu Hurr.” So I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “Sit down and drink,” so I drank, then he said: “Drink,” so I drank, then he said: “Drink,” so I drank, and I continued to drink and he said: “Drink” until I said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I cannot find a way for him.” So he took the cup, thanked God and said his name, then drank it, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but did not They bring it out in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4291 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4292","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The people of the Suffa were seventy. A man who had no cloaks.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Al-Hakim said: “I considered these reports contained in The people of the Suffah, and I found them to be among the greatest companions, may God be pleased with them, for their piety and trust in God Almighty, and their commitment to the service of God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. God Almighty, may God bless him and grant him peace. God Almighty chose him for them as He chose for His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, of poverty, poverty, and supplication for worship. God Almighty, and leave the world to its people, who are the sect to which the Sufis have belonged, century after century, so whoever follows their Sunnah And their patience in abandoning the world and people due to poverty, and refraining from being subjected to questions, they are in every age emulated by the people of character and their Creator. “reliant”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4292 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4293","The sheikh of Sufism in his time, Abu Muhammad Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi, told us. Abu Ahmad al-Jariri told us, he said: I heard Sahl Ibn Abdullah al-Tustari says: “When God Almighty sent the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, there were seven types of people in this world: kings, And he did not command any of them to move from what He is in it, but He commanded them to have knowledge, certainty, piety, and trust in everything they are in.” Sahl, may God have mercy on him, said: “And it should The rational person would say: It is not right for me, after knowing that I am Your servant, to hope and hope for anyone other than You, nor to have any illusions about You, since you created me and shaped me. I am your servant, whether you entrust me to myself or have someone else take care of my affairs.” Al-Hakim said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, described this group as God Almighty singled them out from among the sects with certain qualities, so whoever has those qualities deserves the name of Sufism.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4293 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4294","Abu Amr Uthman bin Abdullah Al-Zahid bin Al-Sammak informed us of the truth in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far Al-Zubarakan told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us. Al-Shafi’i, Al-Walid bin Muslim narrated to us, and Damra bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Humaid, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Iyad bin Suleiman, and it was his Companionship, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best of my nation regarding what the most high-ranking people informed me about is people who laugh out loud.” In the abundance of the mercy of their Lord Almighty, and they cry secretly out of fear of the severity of the punishment of their Lord Almighty, they remember their Lord in the morning and evening. The good houses - the mosques - and they call upon Him with their tongues in hope and fear, and they ask Him with their hands, lowering and raising, and they accept Him with their hearts. Back and forth, their burden upon the people is light, but heavy upon themselves. They move about the earth barefoot on their feet like the crawling of ants, without joy. And no extravagance. They walk quietly, draw near by means, recite the Qur’an, offer the offering, and wear good manners. They must From God Almighty are present witnesses and a watchful eye who discern the servants and contemplate the land. Their souls are in this world and their hearts are in In the Hereafter, they have no concern except for their Imam. They have prepared the preparation for their graves.And to pass on their path and prepare for their station.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {This is for he who fears my position and fears My threat} [Ibrahim: 14] “Al-Hakim said: “Whoever of the Sufis of our time is able to use this description, blessed are he, for he is the one who follows the guidance of those who preceded him. Sufism: a sect of the sects of Muslims. Some of them are good, and some are evil, not as the common people and common people imagine, even if they knew. The replacement of the first class of them with Islam, and their closeness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would have prevented them from much of the conflict between them. As for the people of the elite during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, their names in the reports transmitted to us are different, and if I mentioned all of them, A hadith from it, in its hadith and the context of its text, was mentioned in the book, and some of its chains of narration were not cited in this book, so I mentioned The names of these reports, for the sake of brevity, are Abu Abdullah Al-Farisi and Abu Ubaidah Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah, Abu Al-Yaqzan Ammar bin Yasser, Abdullah bin Masoud Al-Hudhali, and Al-Miqdad bin Amr bin Thalabah, and he was Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghuth adopted him, so it was said that Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad Al-Kindi and Khabab bin Al-Art,Bilal bin Rabah, Suhaib bin Sinan bin Utbah bin Ghazwan, Zayd bin Al-Khattab, Omar’s brother, and Abu Kabsha, the servant of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Marthad Kenaz bin Husayn Al-Adawi, Safwan bin Bayda, Abu Abbas bin Jabr, and Salem, my father’s servant. Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah, Mustah bin Uthaath bin Abbad bin Abdul Muttalib, Ukasha bin Muhsin Al-Asadi, and Masoud Ibn Al-Rabi’ Al-Qari, Umayr Ibn Awf, client of Suhail Ibn Amr, Awaym Ibn Sa’idah, Abu Lubaba Ibn Abd Al-Mundhir, and Salim Ibn Umair bin Thabit, and he was one of the Companions who wept, and about him was revealed: {And their eyes overflowing with tears of grief} [At-Tawbah: 92], and Abu Al-Bishr Ka'b bin Amr, Khubayb bin Yasaf, Abdullah bin Unais, Abu Dharr Jundub bin Junada al-Ghifari, and Utbah bin Masoud Al-Hudhali, and Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them, was among those who would come to them and spend the night with them in the mosque, and Hudhayfah was Bin Al-Yaman was also among those who would come to them and spend the night with them, as well as Abu Al-Darda’ Uwaimir bin Amir, Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Juhani, and Al-Hajjaj bin Amr Al-Aslami, Abu Hurairah Al-Dawsi, Thuban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Muadh bin Al-Harith Al-Qari,Al-Sa’ib bin Khallad, and Thabit bin Wadia’ah, may God be pleased with them all. Al-Hakim, may God be pleased with him, said: “I attributed these names to There are many separate reports in which the people of Suffah and those staying in the mosque with them are mentioned. Among them are those whose migration occurred earlier, such as Ammar bin Yasser, Salman, Bilal, Suhaib, Al-Miqdad, and others, and among them were those whose migration was delayed, so they lived in the mosque among the people of Suffah, and among them was one who converted to Islam in the year of the conquest, then he returned with him and stayed among the people of Suffah, as he did not take people or money to the city, and he is not counted among the people of Suffah. The immigrants, according to his saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no migration after the conquest, but jihad and intention.” And among what I hope for from the grace of God Almighty That everyone who follows their Sunnah in trust and poverty until the Day of Resurrection is one of them, and will be gathered with them, and everyone who loves them, And if he is returning to the world and wealth, then that is hoped for him as well, according to what he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever loves a people will be gathered with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4294 - This is a strange and objectionable hadith"
"4295","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Al-Muthanna told us, Yahya bin Mu’in told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “What happened: O you who have believed, it was revealed in Medina. And whatever happens: “O people, then in Mecca.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4295 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4296","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki’ informed us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We read al-Mufassal for a while, and presented arguments “In Mecca, it is not there, O you who have believed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4296 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
